// A mutable module const IS writable, but its storage is a fixed-capacity static
// buffer. Growing it would allocate a fresh buffer on the GC heap and hang it off
// a global the collector's root set never visits (frames + defers only), so the
// pointee would be freed or moved with the global left dangling — silent
// corruption, no trap.
//
// So the two growth mutators are rejected while the in-place ones stay: `arr[i] = v`
// and `clear` / `remove_last` only touch a buffer that is already there. T3077
// until a global root registry exists.
//
// Note this is NOT T3071: the receiver is genuinely mutable now, so the
// immutable-receiver check no longer fires and nothing else would have caught the
// growth.
module "snippet"

COUNTS: i32[]!: [0, 0]

main :: fn() -> i32 {
    COUNTS[0] = 1
    COUNTS.clear()
    COUNTS.push(2)
    COUNTS.push_all([3, 4])
    return COUNTS[0]
}
